// The same push on a loaded cart: 30 stones (150 kg on an 80 kg cart) dropped in as cargo. The mole leans
// on it as hard as on the empty cart in cart_push_level, but it takes about three times as long to get going,
// and it holds the mole back to its own pace.
map
############################################################
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#.@........................................................#
#==========================================================#
############################################################
end
give Cart 1
place 2 6 0 Cart
// cargo: three stones dropped in from above, then 27 more loaded
drop 3 Stone 6 -1
drop 3 Stone 6 -2
drop 3 Stone 6 -3
expect 20 cargo == 3
load 21 27 Stone
expect 22 cargo == 30
hold 25-110 right
expect 60 cartv < 6               // slower to get going than the empty cart (which is past 6 by now)
expect 60 cartv > 0
expect 60 cartgap > 0             // the mole held behind it
